  "why": "A conventional cast-in-place solid suspended slab is a multi-trade element and must be estimated as its true trades — soffit formwork/shoring, steel fixing and concrete placing/finishing — rather than a single blended concrete rate, because the formwork and reinforcement effort dominate the cost and the labour peaks at different times in the cycle.",
